  "findings": [
    "The seven preview frames and summary have readable labels without observed clipping or overlap.",
    "The axes increase sigma rightward and height upward; local panels use the same scales and label their relative height.",
    "The initial tangent uses dt/dsigma=-Im(zeta prime)/Re(zeta prime), with the screen y direction correctly reversed.",
    "Zero indices 2 and 7 are positive-slope prime-index counterexamples; composite index 8 is negative. Zero 3 and zero 97 match their checked signs.",
    "Index, actual zero height, and integer primality are explicitly distinguished. Pink marks the selected path independently of primality.",
    "The background is the phase of zeta(s)-a at the current target. Neutral masking below 1e-10 avoids assigning a reliable phase to near-zero sampled values.",
    "The moving point is display interpolation between checked samples, as the footer discloses. The initial tangent is not asserted to equal the entire curved path.",
    "The old intro marks held viewport exits as boxes and explicitly says they are not current roots after exit.",
    "The summary correctly tests slope sign, reproduces 14/11 prime-index and 35/39 composite-index counts, and states that the critical-line seeds do not prove RH.",
    "The original-start preview now shows target a=0 and the unadvanced starting roots."
  ],
